course: dictionary
lesson: 2873
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, look at the clues around the word. «Donkeys bray to call other donkeys, and the sound can carry about 3 kilometres across their desert homeland.» The bray and the desert tell you that donkey means the animal here.
explain: Now read this: «Don't be a donkey!» There is no animal in the sentence, and the speaker is calling someone silly. So donkey means a silly or stupid person. This meaning is informal, so use it with care, because it can sound rude.
explain: Some words are part of a phrase, and the phrase has its own meaning. «We have waited donkey's years for the bus.» The words donkey's years do not mean a number of donkeys. They mean a very long time. Always ask: does my meaning fit the whole sentence?
fact: Donkey has three meanings: an animal, a silly person (informal, mildly rude), and donkey's years.
fact: A donkey is an animal like a small horse, with long ears and a loud bray.
fact: «Bray» means the loud cry a donkey makes.
fact: «Donkey work» means dull, hard work, and «donkey's years» means a very long time.
fact: Donkeys are relatives of horses, and «donkeys form strong friendships» with each other.
exercise: «Donkeys bray to call other donkeys.» What does bray mean here? | A long, thin tail | *A loud cry or call | A soft purr | A kind of food
exercise: Mia shouts, «Don't be a donkey!» to her brother who dropped the cake. What does donkey mean here? | *A silly or stupid person | A friend of a horse | An animal with long ears | A very long time
exercise: Dad says, «We have waited donkey's years for the bus.» What does donkey's years mean? | Exactly three years | *A very long time | A donkey's birthday | Only one minute
test: Which phrase means dull, hard work? | Stubborn as a donkey | *Donkey work | Donkey ride | Donkey's years
test: «When worried, a donkey tends to freeze and think rather than run, which people call stubborn.» What does stubborn mean? | Hungry | Very kind | *Refusing to move or change your mind | Very fast
exam: In «Donkey coats are not waterproof», what does waterproof mean? | Made of wood | Loves to swim | Full of water | *Keeps water out
